 ## Lifetime
 
 Each request renews the session for 30 minutes, `EXPIRY_MINUTES` in `larder/sessions.py`. Until March 2024 the limit
@@ -9,8 +12,14 @@ minutes, the shortest that ended those tickets.
 
 ## Storage
 
-Sessions live in Postgres ([keep sessions in the database](../adr/0001-keep-sessions-in-the-database.md)).
+Sessions live in a dictionary in each web process. Requests in that process use the shared
+[`session_store`](../../larder/session_store.py) instance, which implements `get` and `put` without a database
+connection. Reads and writes copy session data; callers save changes with `put`.
 
-## Shaped by
+## Known limits
 
-- [Keep sessions in the database](../adr/0001-keep-sessions-in-the-database.md)
+- Processes do not share sessions. When larder moved to two servers in 2023, requests reaching another server
+  logged members out; Postgres storage previously resolved this. Routing a member's requests to the same process
+  avoids those logouts while that process runs.
+- Restarts and deploys discard sessions and require members to log in again. Volunteers previously avoided
+  deploying during opening hours for this reason; schedule restarts outside opening hours to limit disruption.
